# RTL sidebar / workspace shell

Canonical shell: `components/sidebar.tsx` + `components/workspace-shell.tsx`.

## Layout contract (do not break)

- Aside is `fixed inset-y-0 start-0 z-[60] w-[min(15.5rem,85vw)]`.
- Main content **must** offset with matching inline-start space at `md+`: `md:ms-[15.5rem]` (or `padding-inline-start` / equivalent equal to **15.5rem**). If width changes in the aside, update the shell offset in the same change.
- **Never** ship a fixed/visible sidebar without that offset — content under the aside is unreadable and is a regression the team will not tolerate.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — fixed aside + matching main offset
<aside className="fixed … start-0 w-[min(15.5rem,85vw)] …" />
<div className="min-h-dvh md:ms-[15.5rem]">…</div>

// ❌ BAD — fixed aside, no md+ inline-start offset (covers dashboard)
<aside className="fixed … start-0 w-[15.5rem]" />
<div className="min-h-dvh">…</div>
```

## Mobile vs desktop

- **Mobile:** drawer **closed by default**; backdrop only while open (`md:hidden`); dismissible. Overlay covering content is OK only when the drawer is open.
- **Desktop (`md+`):** sidebar always visible and **clickable** — must **not** be `inert` / `aria-hidden` incorrectly. Use something like `drawerActive = mobileOpen || isDesktop` so `inert` applies only when the mobile drawer is closed.
- Fix **both** constraints together: readable main content **and** working nav. Never “fix” overlap by making the desktop aside inert, or “fix” inert by removing the content offset.

## QA before shipping any sidebar/shell change

- Verify on **https://arabicbuzz.netlify.app/** only (never localhost).
- Check ~**375px** (drawer closed; content full-width under top bar) and ~**1280px** (sidebar + dashboard text both fully readable and nav clickable).
